@startuml
autonumber

actor User
participant "Identity Broker (Keycloak)" as IB
participant "Foreign IdP" as FIDP
participant "API Gateway" as API
actor "Back Office User" as BO
participant "User Directory" as UD
participant "User Directory\nSynchronization Service" as UDSS


== Identity Brokering Configuration ==

User -> IB: Configure brokering (urls, credentials)

note right of IB #yellow
**Identity Brokering Configuration**
end note

IB -> IB: Setup configuration to map claims from Foreign IdP to user model of Identity Broker

note right of IB #yellow
**Setup configuration**\nto map claims from Foreign IdP to Identity Broker\nand verify Foreign IdP JWT
end note

IB -> IB: Configure issuer and essential claim verification

IB -> IB: Configure First Login Flow

note right of IB #yellow
**Configure First Login Flow**\nChange default "First Broker Login Flow"\nto disable automatic user creation\nand create a new session if user exists.
end note

== User Creation - Manual/API ==

BO -> UD: Create/Modify/Delete User\nhaving common identifier\nin User Directory & Foreign IdP

note right of UD #yellow
**User Creation - Manual/API**\nCreate/Modify/Delete User having common identifier\nin User Directory & Foreign IdP
end note

== Automated User Creation (using User Directory Synchronization Service) ==

loop forever
    UDSS -> UD: Listen for changes (user created/modified/deleted)
    alt If change in user directory
        UD -> UDSS: Create/Modify/Delete User\nhaving common identifier\nin User Directory & Foreign IdP
    end alt
end loop

note right of UDSS #yellow
**Automated User Creation**\nListen for changes and sync users between\nUser Directory & Foreign IdP
end note

== Configuring API Gateway ==

IB -> API: Share Public Key to configure authentication

note right of API #yellow
**Configuring API Gateway**\nShare Public Key to configure authentication
end note

API -> API: Configure protected routes\nto require token signed by private key\nof Identity Broker

== Authentication Flow ==

User -> API: Request Authentication
API -> User: Redirect
User -> FIDP: Authenticate
FIDP -> API: Authentication Response (Foreign IdP Token)

alt if user exists
    API -> IB: Fetch user detail and create session
    IB -> API: Translate Foreign IdP token and return R3 Platform native token
end alt

note right of API #yellow
**Translate Foreign IdP IdM token**\nand return R3 Platform native token
end note

API -> User: Authentication Response (Token)

alt User not registered
    API -> User: Unauthorized
end alt

== Resource Access Flow ==

User -> API: Request Resource (with Token)
API -> API: Check token signature

alt If public key known OR token not expired
    API -> User: Resource
else
    API -> User: Unauthorized
end alt

note right of API #yellow
**Resource Access Flow**\nCheck token signature to grant or deny access
end note

@enduml
